course: dictionary
lesson: 11189
title: Wispy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wispy describes something thin, light and fine, made of small loose strands. You can see its shape, but it looks delicate, like a few threads of hair blowing in the wind.
explain: Read the words around it to find the meaning. «Cirrus clouds are thin wispy clouds of ice high in the sky.» The clues are thin and high in the sky, so wispy must mean thin and light, not heavy or dark.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Her wispy hair blew across her face» still makes sense with thin and fine. Try heavy or dark instead, and the sentence stops making sense.
fact: Wispy means thin, light and fine, in small loose strands.
fact: «Wispy clouds» are high clouds made of ice crystals, called cirrus clouds.
fact: «Wispy smoke» drifts up from a chimney, thin and easy to see through.
fact: «Wispy beard» describes a beard that is thin and soft.
fact: Wispy changes form when you compare: wispier means more thin and light, and wispiest means the most thin and light.
exercise: What does wispy mean in «Cirrus clouds are thin wispy clouds of ice high in the sky»? | Dark and heavy | Hot and sticky | Loud and fast | *Thin and light, like loose strands
exercise: Which phrase describes thin, soft hair? | Bright sunshine | *Wispy hair | Heavy rain
exercise: Which thing is most likely to be wispy? | A heavy stone | *Smoke drifting from a chimney | A brick wall
test: «The old man had a wispy beard and a kind smile.» What does wispy mean here? | Very long and tangled | Coloured bright red | *Thin and soft | Thick and curly
test: Ella says wispy clouds are thick and grey. Is she right? | No, they are wispy only when they are dark | Yes, because grey always means wispy | *No, wispy clouds are thin and light, made of ice crystals | Yes, they are thick and grey
exam: Which sentence uses wispy correctly? | The bread was wispy and hard | The wispy engine roared loudly | The rock was wispy and heavy | *The mist was wispy, with thin strands drifting over the field
